IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bsma-types`

-- Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 — GOALS 5 AND 6.
--
--   Goal 5: "May a Strata Titles Board hear this and make this order; when
--            does its order take effect and how long does an interim order
--            last?"
--   Goal 6: "Is this an offence, and what is the most it can cost; may it be
--            compounded; and when is a notice served?"
--
-- Source: ../source/BSMA2004.txt — Part 6 (ss 89-120), Part 8 (ss 123-139),
-- and the offence provisions throughout.

§ `Goal 5 — Strata Titles Boards`

-- s 89(3): a Board is "the president or a deputy president; and ... 2 or 4
-- members selected by the president".
@ref s 89(3)
GIVEN `presided by the president or a deputy` IS A BOOLEAN, members IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is properly constituted, presided:` `presided by the president or a deputy` `, members` members IF
    `presided by the president or a deputy` AND (members EQUALS 2 OR members EQUALS 4)

-- s 92(1)(b): if mediation fails "at the end of a period ... of not more than
-- 3 days of mediation", the Board arbitrates. (9): a final order "within
-- 6 months from the date it is constituted or within such extension ... as
-- the Minister may grant".
@ref s 92(1)(b)
GIVEN `days of mediation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `mediation is within its limit, days` `days of mediation` IF `days of mediation` AT MOST 3

@ref s 92(9)
GIVEN constituted IS A DATE, `extended to` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Board's final order is due by, constituted` constituted `, extended to` `extended to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `extended to`
    WHEN JUST e  THEN e
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` constituted 6

-- s 101(4)-(5): where the corporation has a discretion, it is taken to refuse
-- only if it has decided not to act — and is deemed to have decided so if,
-- "before the expiry of 2 months after the making of the application", it
-- neither acts nor tells the applicant. (6): no order on a matter needing a
-- unanimous, special, 90%, comprehensive or consensus resolution.
@ref s 101(4)-(6)
GIVEN `application made` IS A DATE, `acted or told the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation is deemed to have refused, applied` `application made` `, acted or answered:` `acted or told the applicant` `, as at` `as at` IF
    (NOT `acted or told the applicant`) AND `as at` AT LEAST `add months` `application made` 2

@ref s 101(6)
GIVEN k IS A `Resolution kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Board may order on a power exercised by` k IF
    k EQUALS `an ordinary resolution`

-- s 101(8): a defect is presumed to be in the lot or common property above if
-- there is dampness, moisture or water penetration on the ceiling (or its
-- finishing) of the interior below, "in the absence of proof to the contrary".
@ref s 101(8)
GIVEN `dampness on the ceiling below` IS A BOOLEAN, `proof to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defect is taken to be in the unit above, dampness:` `dampness on the ceiling below` `, proof to the contrary:` `proof to the contrary` IF
    `dampness on the ceiling below` AND (NOT `proof to the contrary`)

-- s 103(2): the Board must not refuse to invalidate unless "(a) ... the failure
-- ... did not prejudicially affect any person; and (b) ... compliance ... would
-- not have resulted in a failure to pass the resolution, or have affected the
-- result of the election".
@ref s 103(2)
GIVEN `no one was prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN, `compliance would not have changed the result` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may refuse to invalidate, no prejudice:` `no one was prejudiced` `, same result:` `compliance would not have changed the result` IF
    `no one was prejudiced` AND `compliance would not have changed the result`

-- s 104(2): an application to nullify a resolution where a vote was denied or
-- notice not given "may not be made after 21 days after the date of the
-- meeting".
@ref s 104(2)
GIVEN meeting IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to nullify a resolution, meeting` meeting MEANS meeting PLUS 21

-- s 116: the Board "may dismiss" on any of grounds (a)-(e).
@ref s 116
GIVEN gs IS A LIST OF `Dismissal ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may dismiss the application on` gs IF NOT (gs EQUALS EMPTY)

-- s 118(1)(b): renewal if requested "not later than 3 months after the order
-- is made". (5): it lasts "(a) until the expiry of any period, not exceeding
-- 3 months, ... specified in the order ...; (b) if application is duly made
-- for its renewal, until the renewal is granted or refused; or (c) if it is
-- renewed, until the expiry of a period of 6 months, starting with the making
-- of the order".
@ref s 118(1)(b), (5)
GIVEN o IS AN `Interim order facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interim order is in force,` o IF
        o's `as at` AT LEAST o's `made on`
    AND BRANCH IF o's `renewed`                          THEN o's `as at` LESS THAN `add months` (o's `made on`) 6
               IF `renewal duly requested` AND (NOT o's `renewal decided`) THEN TRUE
               OTHERWISE                                     o's `as at` LESS THAN `add months` (o's `made on`) `the specified period`
    WHERE
        `the specified period` MEANS IF o's `period specified in months` GREATER THAN 3 THEN 3 ELSE o's `period specified in months`
        `renewal duly requested` MEANS
            CONSIDER o's `renewal requested on`
            WHEN JUST r  THEN r AT MOST `add months` (o's `made on`) 3
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 119(4): an order "takes effect when a copy ... is served on (a) the
-- applicant; (b) the management corporation ...; and (c) the person against
-- whom the order is made" — so on the last of the three.
@ref s 119(4)
GIVEN `served on the applicant` IS A DATE, `served on the corporation` IS A DATE, `served on the respondent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Board's order takes effect on, applicant` `served on the applicant` `, corporation` `served on the corporation` `, respondent` `served on the respondent` MEANS
    `the later of` `served on the applicant` (`the later of` `served on the corporation` `served on the respondent`)

§ `Goal 6 — offences, penalties, composition and service`

-- The penalty each offence provision states. s 128: an offence "for which no
-- penalty is expressly provided" — a fine not exceeding $10,000 (ss 18(2),
-- 27(4), 28(4), 31(2), 48(3), 68(3), 134(4)). s 136(4): regulations may set
-- up to "$20,000 or ... 12 months or ... both" (lifts and escalators) or
-- "$5,000" (others).
@ref ss 14, 16(4), 17(9)-(10), 20(8), 26(9), 40(10), 48(1A), 60(10), 61(3), 96(2), 118(7), 120(2), 126(6), 127(3), 128, 136(4)
GIVEN o IS A `BSMA offence`
GIVETH A `BSMA penalty`
`the maximum penalty for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 14 selling without an accepted schedule, or changing it`        THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 10000, 12, 0,   TRUE
    WHEN `s 16(4) failing to establish maintenance funds`                    THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 10000, 0,  100, FALSE
    WHEN `s 17(9) maintenance fund payment, trust or accounts duties`        THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 10000, 0,  100, FALSE
    WHEN `s 17(10) inspection, register of purchasers or copy duties`        THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 2000,  0,  100, FALSE
    WHEN `s 20(8) a Commissioner's managing agent failing to pay in or report` THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000, 0,  0,   FALSE
    WHEN `s 26(9) failing to hold the first annual general meeting`          THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000,  0,  100, FALSE
    WHEN `s 40(10) not paying contributions 14 days after a demand`          THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 10000, 0,  100, FALSE
    WHEN `s 48(1A) failing to deliver records, keys or property`             THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000,  0,  0,   FALSE
    WHEN `s 60(10) failing to disclose an interest`                          THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000,  12, 0,   TRUE
    WHEN `s 61(3)(b) a council member's or officer's dishonesty or misuse of position` THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000, 12, 0, TRUE
    WHEN `s 96(2) disobeying a Board summons`                                THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000,  24, 0,   TRUE
    WHEN `s 118(7) a false statement for an interim order`                   THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000,  6,  0,   TRUE
    WHEN `s 120(2) contravening a Board order`                               THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 10000, 60, 0,   TRUE
    WHEN `s 126(6) obstructing or refusing the Commissioner`                 THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 2000,  3,  0,   TRUE
    WHEN `s 127 false information to the Commissioner, or falsifying records` THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000, 6,  0,   TRUE
    WHEN `a lift or escalator regulation (s 136(4)(a))`                      THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 20000, 12, 0,   TRUE
    WHEN `any other regulation (s 136(4)(b))`                                THEN `BSMA penalty` OF 5000,  0,  0,   FALSE
    OTHERWISE                                                                     `BSMA penalty` OF 10000, 0,  0,   FALSE

-- Offences with an excuse written into them: s 26(9) and s 48(1A), (3)
-- "without reasonable excuse"; s 126(6)(b)-(c) likewise; s 27(5) a defence of
-- "all reasonable steps and ... all due diligence". s 127(1): "knowingly or
-- recklessly".
@ref ss 26(9), 27(5), 48(1A), (3), 126(6)(b)-(c)
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reasonable excuse or due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an excusable offence is committed, conduct:` `the conduct` `, excuse or due diligence:` `a reasonable excuse or due diligence` IF
    `the conduct` AND (NOT `a reasonable excuse or due diligence`)

-- s 131(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not
-- exceeding the lower of ... (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine
-- ...; (b) $5,000".
@ref s 131(1)
GIVEN o IS A `BSMA offence`, prescribed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` o `, prescribed:` prescribed MEANS
    IF NOT prescribed THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (IF `half` LESS THAN 5000 THEN `half` ELSE 5000)
    WHERE
        `half` MEANS (`the maximum penalty for` o)'s `fine` DIVIDED BY 2

-- s 129(5): service is deemed "(a)" by fax when receipt is acknowledged; "(b)
-- ... (i) on the 3rd working day after the day the notice ... was posted, if
-- sent by prepaid registered post; (ii) on the 4th working day ..., if sent by
-- ordinary post"; "(c)" on the day of delivery or affixing; "(d)" by
-- electronic communication when it becomes capable of being retrieved. s 2(1):
-- "working day" excludes Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays. The public
-- holidays are an input.
@ref ss 2(1) "working day", 129(5)
GIVEN m IS A `Service mode`, sent IS A DATE, holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the notice is served on, mode` m `, sent` sent `, public holidays` holidays MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `by prepaid registered post` THEN `the nth working day after` sent 3
    WHEN `by ordinary post`           THEN `the nth working day after` sent 4
    OTHERWISE sent
    WHERE
        `a working day` d MEANS `is weekday` d AND NOT (elem d holidays)
        `the nth working day after` d n MEANS
            IF n EQUALS 0 THEN d
            ELSE IF `a working day` (d PLUS 1)
                 THEN `the nth working day after` (d PLUS 1) (n MINUS 1)
                 ELSE `the nth working day after` (d PLUS 1) n

-- s 129(1B): a notice from the corporation to a proprietor by email is not
-- served "(a) unless the notice is also posted ...; and (b) until subsection
-- (5)(b) or (d) first applies".
@ref s 129(1B)
GIVEN `also posted` IS A BOOLEAN, `deemed served by post` IS A DATE, `retrievable by email` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`an emailed notice to a proprietor is served on, also posted:` `also posted` `, post date` `deemed served by post` `, email date` `retrievable by email` MEANS
    IF `also posted`
    THEN JUST (`the earlier of` `deemed served by post` `retrievable by email`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 89(1)-(2), (4)-(5), 90, 91, 92(2)-(8), 93-100, 101(1)-(3), (7), 102, 103(1), 104(1), (3), 105-115, 117, 118(2)-(4), (6), 119(1)-(3), 120(1), (3), 123-125, 126(1)-(5), (7)-(9), 129(1)-(4), (6), 129A, 130, 132-139; Third and Fourth Schedules
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`board and general provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 89-100: the Boards — mediation-arbitration, president and panel, objections to members, protection, procedure, confidentiality, open hearings, reconstitution, representation, no jurisdiction on title, summons and oaths, appeal on a point of law only, registrar"
         "ss 101-115, 117: the orders a Board may make — defects, meetings, invalidation, by-laws, interest rates, contributions (never share values, s 108(4)), insurance, consents, managing agents, information, entry, disputes between corporations, ancillary orders and costs"
         "ss 118-120: interim orders; service of orders; enforcement through a District Court"
         "ss 123-125: other remedies kept; originating applications and debts; officers' liability for corporate offences"
         "ss 126-127: the Commissioner's monitoring powers; self-incrimination"
         "ss 129(1)-(4), 129A, 130, 132-136: methods of service; inaccuracies; jurisdiction; protection; Government; exemptions; amending Schedules; regulations"
         "ss 137-139, Third Schedule (omitted as having had effect), Fourth Schedule: savings and transitional provisions"
